## bound

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":":! bound t = t\n\n:| bound_error t =\n    | EmptyRange\n    | AboveLargest : t * t\n\n:= ^ largest_from \\* t {number}. (p : t) : t =\n    ? p > (limit.max : t) / 6 ?> p |: largest_from (p * 6)\n\n:= largest_bound \\* t {number}. () : t =\n    largest_from 1\n\n:= bound_of \\* t {number}. (max : t) : result (bound t) (bound_error t) =\n    ? max < 1 ?> Error EmptyRange\n    |? max > largest_bound () ?> Error (AboveLargest (max, largest_bound ()))\n    |: Ok (bound max)\n\n:= bound_value \\* t. ((bound max) : bound t) : t =\n    max\n\n:= bound_error_text \\* t {number}. (e : bound_error t) : string =\n    ?= e ?|\n    | EmptyRange => \"max must be at least 1\"\n    | AboveLargest (max, largest) => \"max: \" ++# #?max ++# \" is above the largest supported bound \" ++# #?largest\n\n:= dice_count \\* t {number}. (b : bound t) : i32 =\n    := max = bound_value b\n    :~ ^ go (count : i32) (reach : t) : i32 =\n        ? reach >= max ?> count |: go (count + 1) (reach * 6)\n    ? max = 1 ?> 1 |: go 0 1","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  :! bound t = t

  :| bound_error t =
      | EmptyRange
      | AboveLargest : t * t

  := ^ largest_from \* t {number}. (p : t) : t =
      ? p > (limit.max : t) / 6 ?> p |: largest_from (p * 6)

  := largest_bound \* t {number}. () : t =
      largest_from 1

  := bound_of \* t {number}. (max : t) : result (bound t) (bound_error t) =
      ? max < 1 ?> Error EmptyRange
      |? max > largest_bound () ?> Error (AboveLargest (max, largest_bound ()))
      |: Ok (bound max)

  := bound_value \* t. ((bound max) : bound t) : t =
      max

  := bound_error_text \* t {number}. (e : bound_error t) : string =
      ?= e ?|
      | EmptyRange => "max must be at least 1"
      | AboveLargest (max, largest) => "max: " ++# #?max ++# " is above the largest supported bound " ++# #?largest

  := dice_count \* t {number}. (b : bound t) : i32 =
      := max = bound_value b
      :~ ^ go (count : i32) (reach : t) : i32 =
          ? reach >= max ?> count |: go (count + 1) (reach * 6)
      ? max = 1 ?> 1 |: go 0 1
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

#### largest_bound_is_the_largest_power_of_six_of_the_type (test)

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"///- --test\n///> rust\n///> fsharp\n///> typescript\n///> python\n///> lua\n///> c\n///> zig\n///> gleam\n///> pascal\n\n((largest_bound () : i32), (largest_bound () : u64), (largest_bound () : u8))\n|> _assert_eq (362797056i32, 4738381338321616896u64, 216u8)","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

